---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, mailto, OPERATOR } from '../data/site';
---

<Prose
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms for using NiftyFix's free file tools: your responsibilities, what our validation reports mean, and the limits of our liability."
  path="/terms/"
  lede="Plain-language terms for using NiftyFix. By using the site, you agree to them."
  updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
>
  <aside class="panel my-8 p-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 mb-0 grid list-none gap-3 pl-0 text-stone-800 sm:grid-cols-2 dark:text-stone-200">
      <li>✓ The tools are free to use, with no account.</li>
      <li>✓ Your files stay yours and stay on your device.</li>
      <li>
        ✓ Use the tools only for files you have the right to use, and never to forge documents.
      </li>
      <li>✓ Check the official rules before you submit: a passing report is not a guarantee.</li>
    </ul>
  </aside>

  <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    NiftyFix (niftyfix.in) is run by {OPERATOR.name}, {OPERATOR.region} ("we", "us"). These terms
    apply to the website and every tool on it. Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains
    how data is handled. If you do not agree with these terms, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The service</h2>
  <p>
    NiftyFix provides free tools that resize, compress, convert and edit files, and check the result
    against requirements you enter. The tools run in your browser. We may add, change or remove
    tools, and the site may sometimes be unavailable, without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Your files and your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You keep all rights to your files. We do not receive them, so we claim no rights over them.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use the tools only for files you own or are allowed to use, and in line with the law and with
      the rules of the portal or organisation you submit them to.
    </li>
    <li>
      Do not use NiftyFix to forge, falsify or alter official documents, certificates, identity
      documents or signatures you are not authorised to use, or for any other unlawful purpose.
    </li>
    <li>
      Keep your original files. Tools create new files; keeping backups is your responsibility.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. What a validation report means</h2>
  <p>
    A passing report means the file we produced meets the technical requirements you entered, such
    as pixel dimensions, file size and format, as measured from the file itself. It is not a promise
    that any portal, exam body, employer or government office will accept it: they may apply checks
    they do not publish. Always confirm the current requirements from the official source before you
    submit.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Not affiliated</h2>
  <p>
    NiftyFix is an independent service. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or acting for any
    government department, exam authority, recruitment body or other organisation whose requirements
    our tools help you meet. Names of portals and file formats are used only to describe
    compatibility.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Please do not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>attack, overload or try to break the site or its security;</li>
    <li>scrape or copy the site in bulk, or use automated means that degrade it for others;</li>
    <li>present NiftyFix, or files made with it, as official or endorsed by any authority.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Our content and open-source software</h2>
  <p>
    The NiftyFix name, logo, design, text and code are ours, except for third-party open-source
    software and fonts, which are used under their own licences (see{' '}
    <a href="/licenses/">licences</a>
    ). Files you create with the tools are yours.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How the service is provided</h2>
  <p>
    NiftyFix is a free service, offered in good faith and provided "as is" and "as available", and
    you use it at your own discretion. To the fullest extent the law allows, we make no promise,
    express or implied, that the tools will be error-free, uninterrupted, secure or suitable for a
    particular purpose, or that their results will be accepted by anyone else.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for checking every file before you rely on it or submit it anywhere: its
    content, size, dimensions, legibility and format, and that it meets the current official
    requirements. Keep your original files; we cannot recover anything for you, because we never
    receive it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. General information</h2>
  <p>
    Information on this site, including guides, examples, size suggestions and any calculations, is
    general help only. It is not legal, financial, medical, tax or other professional advice, and it
    does not replace the instructions published by the organisation you are applying to.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special or
    consequential loss, or for losses such as a rejected or delayed application, a missed deadline,
    lost opportunities, lost data or lost profits, arising from your use of, or inability to use,
    the site or any file made with it. Where liability cannot be excluded, our total liability to
    you for all claims is limited to one thousand rupees (₹1,000). This does not apply to loss
    caused by our wilful misconduct, or to any liability that cannot be limited under Indian law.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Misuse</h2>
  <p>
    If you use NiftyFix in breach of these terms or the law (for example, to alter a document you
    are not entitled to alter), you agree to be responsible for the consequences and to compensate
    us for any claims, losses or costs that result.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to other websites, portals or services are provided for convenience. We do not control
    them and are not responsible for their content, availability or practices.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version; continuing to use the
    site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of India. Any dispute will be subject to the jurisdiction
    of the courts in Maharashtra, India.
  </p>

  <h2>15. General</h2>
  <p>
    If any part of these terms is found unenforceable, the rest stays in effect. If we do not
    enforce a term straight away, we have not given up the right to do so later. These terms are the
    whole agreement between you and us about the site.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Contact and grievances</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, complaints or notices about these terms: {OPERATOR.name} (grievance officer),{' '}
    <a href={mailto('Terms of use')}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>. We aim to resolve complaints within 30
    days.
  </p>
</Prose>
